# Shell scripts must keep LF endings even when checked out on Windows.
#
# Git's autocrlf would otherwise hand `bash` a file whose `set -o pipefail`
# line ends in CR, and bash fails with "set: pipefail: invalid option name".
# That is why scripts/ci/test-audit-macos-bundle.py could not run on a Windows
# checkout even though it needs neither macOS nor a build: 4 of its 7 cases
# failed on line endings, not on logic.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf
